  "note": "Municipal elections, 20 May 1964. Transcribed from the Belfast Telegraph's provincial results table, read from the page image (the OCR of this page is too defective to use). 'All members Unionist except one. Record poll of 87.53 pc.' The Telegraph lists only the successful candidates; the twelve defeated, with their votes, are added from the returning officer's notice of result in the Mid-Ulster Mail, 23 May 1964, p. 10, and the parties from the same paper's report (p. 1): 24 candidates, 12 Unionists, 10 Ratepayers and 2 Independents, electorate 2,598 and 2,274 votes cast.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page images of the Mid-Ulster Mail, 23 May 1964, pp. 1 and 10 (w8-review, Nov 2026): the twelve defeated candidates are added with the votes the returning officer's notice prints (the report on p. 1 has Fisher 804 and Smyrl 617 against the notice's 844 and 697); the eleven elected Unionists are labelled UUP (were unlabelled); electorate and votes cast recorded."
